@page "/who-i-am-not"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Who I am not";
    ViewData["Description"] = "The other Matteo Fabbris: a professor, a chairman, a journalist, a surfer, a geneticist. I am none of them.";
}

<header class="page-head namesake-head">
    <div>
        <h1>Who I am not</h1>
        <p class="lede">
            Matteo Fabbri is a name I share with a professor, a chairman, a journalist,
            a surfer and a few other people who are frankly more interesting than me.
            This page exists so nobody credits me with their achievements.
        </p>
    </div>
</header>

<p class="namesake-intro">
    If you came here looking for one of them, below is who they are and where to go.
    If you were looking for me, the home page is <a asp-page="/Blog/Index">this way</a>.
</p>

<ol class="namesake-list">
    <li class="namesake">
        <span class="namesake-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <div class="namesake-body">
            <h2>The professor in Ferrara</h2>
            <p class="namesake-role">Teaching and research</p>
            <p>
                A Matteo Fabbri teaches at the University of Ferrara. His official CV
                is online, with qualifications, publications and teaching. If you were
                looking for the professor, he is over there.
            </p>
            <a class="namesake-link" href="https://docente.unife.it/matteo.fabbri1/curriculum-vitae/at_download/file" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                CV on unife.it <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </li>

    <li class="namesake">
        <span class="namesake-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <div class="namesake-body">
            <h2>The entrepreneur</h2>
            <p class="namesake-role">Chairman of GoatAI</p>
            <p>
                This Matteo Fabbri chairs GoatAI, according to his LinkedIn profile.
                A namesake with a company and an important title; I have neither.
            </p>
            <a class="namesake-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/matteo-fabbri-b43225b7/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                LinkedIn profile <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </li>

    <li class="namesake">
        <span class="namesake-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <div class="namesake-body">
            <h2>The journalist at Linkiesta</h2>
            <p class="namesake-role">Current affairs and news</p>
            <p>
                A Matteo Fabbri writes current-affairs articles for Linkiesta.
                His author page collects them all. That is not me: I do not write
                for a newspaper.
            </p>
            <a class="namesake-link" href="https://www.linkiesta.it/author/matteo-fabbri/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                Author page on Linkiesta <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </li>

    <li class="namesake">
        <span class="namesake-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
        <div class="namesake-body">
            <h2>The surfer</h2>
            <p class="namesake-role">Surfboards</p>
            <p>
                A Matteo Fabbri makes surfboards and sells them from his website.
                I am not a champion, and I am not even sure I could stand on a board.
                His site is better than this one, though.
            </p>
            <a class="namesake-link" href="http://matteofabbrisurfboards.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                Matteo Fabbri Surfboards <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </li>

    <li class="namesake">
        <span class="namesake-number" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
        <div class="namesake-body">
            <h2>The geneticist in the Garlasco case</h2>
            <p class="namesake-role">Crime news</p>
            <p>
                A geneticist named Matteo Fabbri is connected to the Garlasco case,
                one of Italy's best-known criminal cases. Donna Glamour has a profile
                of him. That is not me, and I have nothing to do with that story.
            </p>
            <a class="namesake-link" href="https://www.donnaglamour.it/chi-e-matteo-fabbri/curiosita/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                Profile on Donna Glamour <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </li>

    <li class="namesake">
        <span class="namesake-number" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
        <div class="namesake-body">
            <h2>The character in a book</h2>
            <p class="namesake-role">“Tu prepara il filtro”</p>
            <p>
                There is also a Matteo Fabbri in Francesco De Giorgi's book
                “Tu prepara il filtro”. I don't know how big a part he has, but being
                a character in a book is something I envy. He is the only namesake
                I would have liked to be.
            </p>
            <a class="namesake-link" href="https://www.ibs.it/tu-prepara-filtro-libro-francesco-de-giorgi/e/9788849707762" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                The book on IBS <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </li>

    <li class="namesake">
        <span class="namesake-number" aria-hidden="true">07</span>
        <div class="namesake-body">
            <h2>The ad man behind “Una Donna Per Amico”</h2>
            <p class="namesake-role">Television advertising</p>
            <p>
                According to Film.it, a Matteo Fabbri worked on the advertising for
                “Una Donna Per Amico”. A namesake on loan to television. That is not
                me: I work with code, not commercials.
            </p>
            <a class="namesake-link" href="https://www.film.it/news/film/dettaglio/art/da-thomas-a-matteo-17152/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                Article on Film.it <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </li>

    <li class="namesake">
        <span class="namesake-number" aria-hidden="true">08</span>
        <div class="namesake-body">
            <h2>The Opus Dei priest</h2>
            <p class="namesake-role">A Don Matteo Fabbri</p>
            <p>
                On opusdei.org, a Don Matteo Fabbri writes about prayer and how to
                teach it to friends. I am not the head of Opus Dei, I am not a priest,
                and I did not write that article.
            </p>
            <a class="namesake-link" href="https://opusdei.org/it-it/article/insegnare-ai-nostri-amici-a-pregare-don-matteo-fabbri-sullanno-della-fede/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                Article on opusdei.org <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </li>
</ol>

<p class="namesake-note">
    None of them has anything to do with this site, and I am not responsible
    for what they do. The name, for better or worse, is the same.
</p>
